# Grim Hollow Player's Guide 2024 Transformations: Aberrant Horror, Fey, Fiend.
TRANS = {
 "Aberrant Horror": {
  "intro": "You become an Aberration whose body reshapes itself at will. From Stage 1 on, your Boons and Flaws cannot be removed by ordinary or typical magic. Only a Wish-level effect ends the Transformation. You advance a stage when a story event ties into it, such as exposure to unearthly magic, resting near a cursed site or item, answering an Aether Kindred's dream quest, or drinking the fluids of a living Aberration.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "You gain both Stage 1 Boons and the Stage 1 Flaw.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Aberrant Form", "Aberrant Mutation"], "d": "Aberrant Horror stage 1. You become an Aberration and can shift your body into useful mutations."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 2 Boon. You also gain the Stage 2 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Aberrant Horror stage 2. Gain eldritch limb upgrades or writhing tendrils, plus Hideous Appearance."},
   3: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 3 Boon. You also gain the Stage 3 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Aberrant Horror stage 3. Frighten foes or restrain them with tendrils, plus Unstable Existence."},
   4: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 4 Boon. You also gain the Stage 4 Flaw. Entropic Abomination replaces the Stage 3 Flaw, Unstable Existence.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Aberrant Horror stage 4. Channel spell slots into your limbs or poison nearby foes, plus Entropic Abomination."}
  },
  "opt": {
   "Aberrant Form": "Aberration is now one of your creature types, alongside any others. The first time you become Bloodied after a Short or Long Rest, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage.",
   "Aberrant Mutation": "You can take on a mutation a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. Each lasts 1 minute. You can end it early with a Bonus Action or swap to another, which costs another use. All uses return on a Short or Long Rest. **Chitinous Shell.** Bonus Action. If you wear no heavy armor, your AC rises by 2 and your Speed drops by 10 feet. **Eldritch Limbs.** Bonus Action. When you take the Attack action, you can replace attacks with melee attacks using your limbs. You are proficient, use Strength or Dexterity, and deal 1d8 Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage (choose each time you manifest the mutation). You can also make one such attack as a Bonus Action. The limbs cannot hold items and are not weapons or Unarmed Strikes. **Slimy Form.** Bonus Action. You have Advantage on checks to escape a grapple, you can Dash as a Bonus Action, and you resist Acid, Fire, and Cold damage.",
   "Unstable Form": "After a Long Rest that follows a day in which you took damage, roll 1d100 on the Unstable Form table and apply the mutation for your current Transformation Stage. It lasts until your next Long Rest.",
   "Efficient Killer": "Your eldritch limb attacks gain an extra effect from the damage type you chose. **Piercing.** You can replace a limb attack with a hurled barb. You are proficient with it, its range is 20/60, it has the Finesse and Thrown properties, and it deals 2d6 Piercing damage. **Bludgeoning.** The limb ends in a bone club and deals an extra 1d8 Bludgeoning damage. It uses the Slow property and you have Mastery with it. **Slashing.** The limb grows hooked claws and deals an extra 1d8 Slashing damage. It uses the Graze property and you have Mastery with it.",
   "Writhing Tendrils": "As a Bonus Action, tendrils sprout from you for 1 minute. You can retract them with a Bonus Action. You can use this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Short or Long Rest. While they are out, you gain these benefits. **Push Back.** When a creature moves within 5 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to push it. Unless it succeeds on a Strength save, it moves 5 feet away and its Speed is 0 until the start of your next turn. The DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. **Slip Away.** You can Disengage as a Bonus Action. **Ward Off.** When a creature targets you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to give it Disadvantage on all its melee attacks that turn.",
   "Terrifying Visage": "When you use Aberrant Mutation or Writhing Tendrils, you choose one creature within 30 feet that can see you. It must succeed on a Wisdom save or be Frightened for 1 minute. The DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. A creature that succeeds is immune to this effect for 24 hours.",
   "Constricting Tendrils": "Requires Writhing Tendrils. While your tendrils are out, you can use a Bonus Action to try to restrain a creature within 5 feet. It must succeed on a Strength or Dexterity save or be Restrained. The DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. The Restrained creature can use an action for a Strength (Athletics) check against that DC to break free. The condition also ends if you are Incapacitated, you move, you retract the tendrils, or you use them for another ability.",
   "Eldritch Aberration": "Requires spell slots. Once per turn, when you hit with an eldritch limb attack, you can expend a spell slot to add 1d6 damage per slot level. Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Force, Lightning, or Thunder for the extra damage. If any of these dice shows a 6, the target is knocked Prone.",
   "Poison Tendrils": "Requires Writhing Tendrils. You resist Poison damage and are immune to the Poisoned condition. While your tendrils are out, each creature of your choice that starts its turn within 5 feet of you takes 3d6 Poison damage unless it succeeds on a Constitution save. The DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage.",
   "Hideous Appearance (Aberrant Horror)": "Your body is a horror of eyes, bone, or tusks. You can suppress this form and look like the person you once were, but doing so takes effort and fails under stress. The GM can call for a Constitution save when you become Bloodied, concentrate on a spell, fall Unconscious, enter hallowed ground, or choose to reveal yourself. The DC depends on your stage: 13 at Stage 2, 16 at Stage 3, 20 at Stage 4. On a failure your true form shows. Non-evil creatures that see it become Hostile to you unless the GM decides otherwise.",
   "Unstable Existence": "Whenever you roll a natural 1 or 2 on a saving throw against a spell, your Hideous Appearance is revealed and you roll again on the Unstable Form table. If the new result is lower than your current Unstable Form effect, it replaces that effect.",
   "Entropic Abomination": "This Flaw replaces Unstable Existence. Each time you fail a saving throw, and the first time you become Bloodied after a Long Rest, you roll on the Unstable Form table. If the result is lower than your current Unstable Form effect, it replaces that effect."
  }
 },
 "Fey": {
  "intro": "You gain the nature of the Fey and serve one of the four Fey Courts. Spring uses Thunder, Summer uses Fire, Autumn uses Poison, and Winter uses Cold. Your Court shapes several later Boons and Flaws, so keep track of it. You advance a stage through a story event such as striking a bargain with a greater Fey, serving a Fey Queen, founding a faerie ring, defeating a rival Court agent, or winning a title in the Realm of Faerie. Undoing the Transformation is dangerous and rarely works.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "You gain Fey Form and choose one other Stage 1 Boon. You also gain the Stage 1 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": ["Fey Form"], "d": "Fey stage 1. Become Fey and pledge to a Court, gaining a teleporting strike."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 2 Boon. You also gain the Stage 2 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Fey stage 2. Gain a Court visage or free minor spells, plus Queen's Command."},
   3: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 3 Boon. You also gain the Stage 3 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Fey stage 3. Gain a disguise, a manifested natural weapon, or a paralyzing dream, plus Weakened Constitution."},
   4: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 4 Boon. You also gain the Stage 4 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Fey stage 4. Gain greater free spells or invisibility, plus Seasonally Affected."}
  },
  "opt": {
   "Fey Form": "Fey is now one of your creature types, alongside any others. After each Long Rest, choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Psychic, or Thunder. You resist that damage type until your next Long Rest.",
   "Servant of the Spring Court": "Spring favors passion, rebirth, and sowing. Its Fey are fickle and quick to anger, like satyrs and nymphs. As a Bonus Action, you teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. One creature of your choice within 5 feet of your start or end space takes 1d6 Thunder damage. You can use this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.",
   "Servant of the Summer Court": "Summer favors warmth, excess, and vanity. Its Fey are jovial and showy, like dryads and pixies. As a Bonus Action, you teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. One creature of your choice within 5 feet of your start or end space takes 1d6 Fire damage. You can use this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.",
   "Servant of the Autumn Court": "Autumn favors scheming, secrets, and decay. Its Fey, such as treants and other plant Fey, look kind but hide ugly methods. As a Bonus Action, you teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. One creature of your choice within 5 feet of your start or end space takes 1d6 Poison damage. You can use this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.",
   "Servant of the Winter Court": "Winter favors stillness, darkness, and death. Its Fey are serious, cruel, and blunt about their aims. As a Bonus Action, you teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. One creature of your choice within 5 feet of your start or end space takes 1d6 Cold damage. You can use this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.",
   "Two-Faced": "As a Magic action, you show the face of your Court. Creatures within 30 feet that can see you must succeed on a Charisma save or suffer an effect for 1 minute. The DC is 8 plus your Charisma modifier plus your Transformation Stage. You can use this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest. **Spring.** Failed targets are Stunned and repeat a Constitution save at the end of each of their turns. It ends early if you or an ally damages the target or takes other harmful actions against it. **Summer.** Failed targets are Charmed. It ends early if you or an ally damages the target or takes other harmful actions against it. **Autumn.** Failed targets are Poisoned and repeat a Constitution save at the end of each of their turns. **Winter.** Failed targets are Frightened of you. It ends early if the target ends its turn out of your line of sight.",
   "Magic Tricks": "You can cast one cantrip, one level 1 spell, and one level 2 spell from your Court, each once per Long Rest with no slot or components. The spell save DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. **Spring.** Poison Spray, Fog Cloud, Misty Step. **Summer.** Fire Bolt, Burning Hands, Flame Blade. **Autumn.** Shillelagh, Thunderwave, Ray of Enfeeblement. **Winter.** Ray of Frost, Ice Knife, Darkness.",
   "Queen's Command": "You owe your Fey Queen tribute twice a year, at times tied to your Court such as the solstices or equinoxes. If she finds it lacking, you learn so at once and receive instructions to atone. Until you do, you have Disadvantage on D20 Tests. If a week passes without you satisfying her, she pulls you into her Court. You then stay in the Realm of Faerie for 100 years unless you bargain your way out. The GM decides what counts as fitting tribute, such as magic items, secrets, captured Fey criminals, or Humanoid servants.",
   "Illusionary Cloak": "As a Magic action, you wrap yourself in an illusion for up to 1 hour that makes you look like another creature of your size and humanoid shape. It ends if you use a Bonus Action to drop it, die, or become Unconscious. A creature can see through it by taking the Study action and passing a DC 20 Intelligence (Investigation) check.",
   "Tooth and Claw": "As a Bonus Action, you manifest a natural weapon for 1 minute. You can use it in place of any weapon attack, but it is not an Unarmed Strike. It uses Strength or Dexterity, you are proficient, and it deals 1d6 Slashing damage plus that modifier. After you take the Attack action without using it, you can use it once as a Bonus Action later that turn. Once per round when it hits, you can deal an extra 2d6 Psychic damage, and the target must succeed on a Constitution save or be Stunned until the end of its next turn. The DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. You can add this extra effect a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage, regaining all uses on a Long Rest.",
   "Dreams and Nightmares": "As a Bonus Action, choose a Humanoid you can see within 30 feet. It must succeed on a Wisdom save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute, caught in a blissful dream or a nightmare. The DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. The target repeats the Constitution save at the end of each of its turns and whenever it takes damage. You can concentrate on the effect like a spell, and if you do, the target has Disadvantage on that save. You can use this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.",
   "Greater Magic Tricks": "Requires Magic Tricks. You can cast one level 3, one level 4, and one level 5 spell from your Court, each once per Long Rest with no slot or components. The spell save DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. **Spring.** Stinking Cloud, Vitriolic Sphere, Cloudkill. **Summer.** Fireball, Fire Shield, Dream. **Autumn.** Lightning Bolt, Blight, Hold Monster. **Winter.** Vampiric Touch, Ice Storm, Cone of Cold.",
   "Twilight Glamour": "As a Magic action, you become Invisible for 1 hour or until you end it with a Bonus Action. If you make an attack roll, deal damage, or cast a spell that forces a saving throw, the remaining time becomes 1 minute. You can use this twice and regain all uses on a Long Rest.",
   "Planar Binding (Fey)": "The magic of Faerie has left you more vulnerable to magic. After a Short or Long Rest, you have Disadvantage on the first saving throw you make against a spell from an enemy.",
   "Weakened Constitution": "The first time you become Bloodied after rolling Initiative, you must succeed on a DC 20 Constitution save or gain a level of Exhaustion. As a Magic action, you can spend Hit Point Dice equal to your Transformation Stage to remove one level of Exhaustion gained this way. Those dice give you no other benefit.",
   "Seasonally Affected": "You have Disadvantage on Death Saving Throws as your Court tries to claim your soul. You also gain Vulnerability based on your Court, and you cannot benefit from Resistance or Immunity to that damage. **Spring.** Necrotic. **Summer.** Cold. **Autumn.** Radiant. **Winter.** Fire."
  }
 },
 "Fiend": {
  "intro": "You become a Fiend through a bargain, a ritual, or a life of cruelty. The change is hard to undo. Only a deed of great sacrifice or atonement lets Wish-level magic remove it. You advance a stage when a story event occurs, such as defeating a greater rival Fiend, ensnaring a powerful soul with a contract, founding a cult, opening a portal to the Netherworld, or killing or corrupting a Seraph. Devilish Contractor ties into Gifts of Damnation, which you earn by signing mortals to contracts.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "You gain Fiendish Soul and choose one other Stage 1 Boon. You also gain the Stage 1 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": ["Fiendish Soul"], "d": "Fiend stage 1. Become a Fiend with a chosen resistance and a contract or smite power."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 2 Boon. You also gain the Stage 2 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Fiend stage 2. Brand foes or improve your contracts, plus Fiend Form."},
   3: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 3 Boon. You also gain the Stage 3 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Fiend stage 3. Hold two Gifts or strengthen your brand, plus Pull of the Netherworld."},
   4: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 4 Boon. You also gain the Stage 4 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Fiend stage 4. Gain fiendish resistance, summon Fiends, or control branded foes, plus True Name."}
  },
  "opt": {
   "Fiendish Soul": "Fiend is now one of your creature types, alongside any others. You have Advantage on Charisma (Deception) checks. Choose Acid, Cold, or Fire and gain Resistance to it. Remember this choice, since other Boons use it.",
   "Infernal Smite": "Once on each of your turns, you can pick one creature you just damaged with a weapon attack, an Unarmed Strike, or a cantrip. It takes extra damage of the type you chose for Fiendish Soul (Acid, Cold, or Fire). You can add this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage, no more than once per damage roll, and regain all uses on a Short or Long Rest. The extra damage is 1d6 at Stage 1 and grows by 1d6 per stage, to 2d6 at Stage 2, 3d6 at Stage 3, and 4d6 at Stage 4.",
   "Devilish Contractor": "You can bind a mortal Humanoid's soul to you with a contract. The mortal gets the gift they ask for, and you gain a Gift of Damnation of your choice. The contract needs magical ink and paper worth 10 GP per Transformation Stage you have reached. Both parties must sign willingly and know the costs. Once signed, you gain the Gift and the mortal gets their wish within 7 days, supplied by the Netherworld. You cannot benefit from the mortal's gift, and neither can an ally. No ally can sign a contract with you. You can take Gifts of your current stage or lower. There is no limit on contracts, but only one Gift is active at a time. A new Gift can replace the active one. After a Long Rest, you can swap your active Gift for any Gift from a contract you have signed.",
   "Daemonic Brand": "As a Bonus Action, you brand a creature you can see within 60 feet with a fiery mark for 1 minute. The target avoids it with a successful Wisdom save. The DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. On a failure, you choose one effect for the duration. The creature takes a -2 penalty on saving throws. Or the first attack against it each turn has Advantage. Or it cannot regain Hit Points. You can use this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.",
   "Enhanced Contract": "Requires Devilish Contractor. You can switch your active Gift of Damnation at the end of a Short or Long Rest. When you switch Gifts, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to 5 times your Transformation Stage.",
   "Devilish Subcontractor": "Requires Enhanced Contract. You can have two Gifts of Damnation active at the same time. You can still switch only one Gift after a Short or Long Rest.",
   "Overwhelming Brand": "Requires Daemonic Brand. Choose one extra effect for a creature under your brand. Its Speed is halved and you can move it up to 10 feet horizontally on your turn at no action cost. Or it is Blinded, and on your turn you can remove the condition at no action cost.",
   "Abyssal Resistance": "You become immune to the damage type you chose for Fiendish Soul and resist the other two of Acid, Cold, and Fire. You also resist damage from nonmagical weapon attacks and Unarmed Strikes.",
   "Infernal Summons": "As a Magic action, you open a portal to the Netherworld and summon up to four Fiends of CR 4 or lower within 30 feet. They stay for 1 minute or less, and the GM decides which Fiends answer. They are Friendly to you and your companions and act right after you in initiative. They follow your spoken commands at no action cost. Without commands, they Dodge and take no other movement, Bonus Action, or Reaction unless it protects themselves.",
   "Ultimate Brand": "Requires Overwhelming Brand. When a creature under your Daemonic Brand starts its turn, you can use your Reaction to dictate its movement and action. The creature then repeats the original Wisdom save at the end of that turn. On a success, you cannot use this Reaction again while the brand lasts.",
   "Fiend Bound": "Your body and soul are tied to the Netherworld, which tries to drag you in. You have Disadvantage on Death Saving Throws.",
   "Fiend Form": "Your skin turns red and leathery, and horns, teeth, and nails erupt from it. You can suppress this form and look like your former self, but it takes effort and fails under stress. The GM can call for a Constitution save when you become Bloodied, concentrate on a spell, fall Unconscious, enter hallowed ground, meet Celestials or other Fiends, or choose to reveal yourself. The DC depends on your stage: 13 at Stage 2, 16 at Stage 3, 20 at Stage 4. On a failure your true form shows. Non-evil creatures will usually become Hostile to you unless the GM decides otherwise.",
   "Pull of the Netherworld": "Whenever you roll a natural 1 on a D20 Test, you take 6d6 Psychic damage as the Netherworld tries to unbind your soul. This happens only once per Short Rest and ignores Resistance and Immunity. If it drops you to 0 Hit Points, you die and your soul goes to the Netherworld. Only a spell of level 7 or higher can return you to life.",
   "True Name": "The Netherworld gives you a new name, your True Name, and a brimstone and brass talisman inscribed with it in Infernal. A creature of CR 10 or higher within 10 feet that knows the name can speak it as a Magic action. You must succeed on a DC 20 Charisma save or suffer these effects for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of your turns. You are Charmed, even if you are immune to it. The speaker can use a Bonus Action to make you move up to your Speed and use your action to attack with a weapon or Unarmed Strike or cast a cantrip at a target they choose. Attacks against you have Advantage and you have Disadvantage on saving throws. You cannot regain Hit Points or have Temporary Hit Points, and you lose any you have."
  }
 }
}
